    <div class="content">
      <p>Hi, I'm Joe Carlo Jr. O. Barandon — a third-year BS Computer Science student at Ateneo de Naga University, currently splitting my time between machine learning and application development. I like building things end to end: from database schema to UI, from a rough idea to something people can actually click through.</p>
      <p>Right now I work as a Junior Applications Programmer at Ateneo de Naga University, contributing to the school's smart campus initiatives, and I've helped train multilingual LLMs as a freelance writing consultant for Outlier. I'm also part of Calamity Crew, a student-led development team where I work on UI/UX and feature implementation for school and regional competitions.</p>
      <p>Some of what I've built: BayanWorks, a community-based job finder platform; StayConnect, a MERN-stack vacation rental booking app; ShopTeneo, a merch tracker for school departments; and Calamity Dash, a 3D game collection with a full UI/UX layer I designed from scratch. That last project placed First overall at Ateneo de Naga's Software Festival 2025, and I was later a National Finalist in DOST's Level Up 2.0 Esports Game Dev Challenge.</p>
      <p>This blog is where I write about what I'm building and learning along the way — including this site itself, which started as a class assignment and became a running experiment in shipping real, working software.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

